## 💧 Why It Matters

The **"Why It Matters"** section highlights four major effects of improper waste disposal.

### 💧 Water Pollution

Improperly disposed waste can contaminate bodies of water and negatively affect the surrounding environment.

### 🌱 Soil Contamination

Waste and potentially harmful substances can affect soil quality and the condition of the surrounding environment.

### 🦟 Disease-Vector Breeding

Accumulated waste and stagnant water can create environments where disease-carrying organisms can multiply.

### 🌊 Flooding

Waste can clog drainage systems and contribute to flooding, especially during periods of heavy rainfall.

I used **individual boxes with icons** for each effect so that the information would be organized, easy to scan, and visually balanced.

---

## 📱 Our Proposed Solution

The main solution presented in the infographic is a:

> **"Smart Waste Reporting & Monitoring System"**

I designed it as a **technology-based platform** that allows residents to report waste-related problems while helping local authorities monitor and manage those reports.

### 🔄 Proposed System Flow

**Report → Location Mapping → Collection Schedule → Report Status Tracking → Monitoring Dashboard**

### 📍 Report

Residents can report waste-related problems they observe in their community.

### 🗺️ Location Mapping

Reports can include location information to help identify where the waste problem is occurring.

### 📅 Collection Schedule

The system can provide information about waste collection schedules to help residents manage and dispose of their waste properly.

### 📌 Report Status Tracking

Residents can check the progress or status of the reports they submitted.

### 📊 Monitoring Dashboard

Local authorities can use a dashboard to monitor reports and identify waste-management concerns that need attention.

